(* Variant tls443-cert: the session handshake over TLS 1.3 on TCP 443, as the code has it, against an attacker that holds
   the key of the certificate of the server (AUD-5, #389). This is the middlebox of ADR-0023 in the best position that it
   can have: it presents the pinned certificate and terminates the TLS session of the client, and opens a session of its
   own to the server. The binding of the Noise handshake to the exporter is what must stop it. *)

process
  ( Setup()
  | LeakCertServer()
  | Sessions(pin_on, bt_export, plabel_session, lab_exp_session, suite_hfs)
  )
